<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman ups Stakis to &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman ups Stakis to &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British hotel operator Stakis Plc was raised to &quot;buy&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot; at Lehman, the investment bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>Lehman said it set a 12-month share price target of 120p on the stock, arguing that the group had proven itself well capable of absorbing acquisitions and enhancing return on capital.</p>
<p>Analyst Fraser Ramzan at the investment bank said in a research note he expected the company to deliver 15 percent annual earnings growth.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 17 1542 4367</p>
